assuming it is the latest mainline. The relevant problems also remain in
the newer input tree at 8e16f8bbf1bd528975fd6f4081eaf00513c1d83e; its
intervening NFC changes are allocation-helper conversions.

Removing an open controller calls nci_unregister_device(), which invokes
the driver's close callback. Holding info_lock across unregister causes
recursive acquisition of that mutex. Patch 1 moves unregister outside it.

The I2C IRQ must also be drained before NCI state is freed, while remaining
available for the closing CORE_RESET response. Patch 2 adds an optional
transport stop_rx callback between unregister and final cleanup/free. It
tracks successful IRQ registration so the existing probe-error unwind
does not release an unowned IRQ. No intermediate patch that drains receive
before unregister is exported.

The series changes only the driver core, I2C transport and private header.
It preserves upstream ISO15693 support, ENXIO handling, firmware strscpy,
ID-table changes, and the existing failed-probe cleanup. Optional reference
clock support, its binding and the Fx0 board description are separate work.

Validation:
- Six host tests pass nine lifecycle cases and reject six independent
  ordering, recursive-lock, callback-wiring and IRQ-ownership controls under
  AddressSanitizer/UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer. Sixteen actual driver/NCI
  callback bodies and their actual type/table wiring are retained. Only
  clock-related model state is omitted for this clock-free fixes series.
- The tests model services, queues, scheduling, the completion wait and an
  NCI 1.x reset response. They exercise no hardware or live kernel endpoint.
  Real elapsed timeout, NCI 2.x notification timing, concurrent firmware
  work and physical IRQ timing are not qualified.
- Clang 21.1.8 ARM W=1 core/I2C/firmware object checks pass on the base and
  both prefixes: nine objects, no compiler diagnostics. KCFI and compressed
  DWARF5 remain enabled, with actual callback type words inspected. Adapting
  the earlier Fx0 config emits two olddefconfig conversion notices for
  IPV6 and NETFILTER_NETLINK.
- Strict checkpatch reports zero findings on both patches, with only DCO
  sign-off checking disabled. Both exported prefix trees replay exactly.

Full kernel/module links, GCC, networking allyesconfig/allmodconfig builds,
and hardware open/unregister, RF, suspend and reliability remain untested.
Earlier Fx0 cold-lifecycle results do not qualify this open-removal path.
The private operations layout changes, so any eventual module qualification
must rebuild and validate the complete matching module cohort.

